# Thread-Safe LRU Cache in Rust

Here's an implementation using a `HashMap` for O(1) lookups combined with an intrusive doubly-linked list for O(1) recency tracking, all guarded by a `Mutex`:

```rust
use std::collections::HashMap;
use std::hash::Hash;
use std::ptr;
use std::sync::Mutex;

struct Node<K, V> {
    key: K,
    value: V,
    prev: *mut Node<K, V>,
    next: *mut Node<K, V>,
}

pub struct LruCache<K, V> {
    map: HashMap<K, *mut Node<K, V>>,
    head: *mut Node<K, V>, // most recently used
    tail: *mut Node<K, V>, // least recently used
    capacity: usize,
}

